{"jobs":[{"id":"b58963f4-8436-4f12-9dca-d17ccee8456d","title":"Behavioral Health Care Manager - Mandarin Speaking","department":"Providers","team":"Providers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-16T15:23:11.656+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/b58963f4-8436-4f12-9dca-d17ccee8456d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/b58963f4-8436-4f12-9dca-d17ccee8456d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Protocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Through a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will be doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform other duties as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted, and independent license to provide mental health treatment from at least one US state. Will consider pre-licensed candidates for Pacific and Mountain time zones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plus if certified proficient for practice in Spanish or Mandarin.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A 401k to save for you future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Malpractice insurance covered by us!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This posting is part of our evergreen talent pipeline. We welcome resumes year-round because we frequently open new positions for this role as we grow. Even if we are not hiring at this exact moment, submitting your application now allows our recruiters to review your experience, keep you top-of-mind, and reach out quickly when the next opening becomes available. If you’re a strong match, we’ll contact you to discuss timing and next steps—otherwise we’ll keep your information on file and revisit it each time a new need arises.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Protocol Behavioral Health\n\nProtocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.\n\nAbout the role\n\nThrough a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\n - Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.\n\n - Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.\n\n - Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.\n\n - Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.\n\n - Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist\n\n - Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.\n\n - Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.\n\n - Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.\n\n - Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.\n\n - Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.\n\n - (If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).\n\n - Perform other duties as assigned.\n\nWhat we are looking for\n\n - Active, unrestricted, and independent license to provide mental health treatment from at least one US state. Will consider pre-licensed candidates for Pacific and Mountain time zones.\n\n - Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.\n\n - Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.\n\n - Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.\n\n - Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.\n\n - Plus if certified proficient for practice in Spanish or Mandarin.\n\nHow we support you\n\n - Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care\n\n - We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - A 401k to save for you future\n\n - Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need\n\n - Malpractice insurance covered by us!\n\n - We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients\n\nWorking days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.\n\nThis posting is part of our evergreen talent pipeline. We welcome resumes year-round because we frequently open new positions for this role as we grow. Even if we are not hiring at this exact moment, submitting your application now allows our recruiters to review your experience, keep you top-of-mind, and reach out quickly when the next opening becomes available. If you’re a strong match, we’ll contact you to discuss timing and next steps—otherwise we’ll keep your information on file and revisit it each time a new need arises.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$55K – $75K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$55K - $75K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"606b7856-b6ef-4c0d-90b6-f14ea6bb07ad","tierSummary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0352ba9d-76b8-4b28-8072-45549ece3093","summary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}},{"id":"81c81b50-4e30-43c6-bea5-c4595dbba8ca","title":"Behavioral Health Care Manager - Spanish Speaking","department":"Providers","team":"Providers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-17T21:12:48.159+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/81c81b50-4e30-43c6-bea5-c4595dbba8ca","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/81c81b50-4e30-43c6-bea5-c4595dbba8ca/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Protocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Through a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will be doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform other duties as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted, and independent license to provide mental health treatment from at least one US state. Will consider pre-licensed candidates for Pacific and Mountain time zones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spanish speaking and able to provide care in Spanish</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A 401k to save for you future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Malpractice insurance covered by us!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This posting is part of our evergreen talent pipeline. We welcome resumes year-round because we frequently open new positions for this role as we grow. Even if we are not hiring at this exact moment, submitting your application now allows our recruiters to review your experience, keep you top-of-mind, and reach out quickly when the next opening becomes available. If you’re a strong match, we’ll contact you to discuss timing and next steps—otherwise we’ll keep your information on file and revisit it each time a new need arises.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Protocol Behavioral Health\n\nProtocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.\n\nAbout the role\n\nThrough a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\n - Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.\n\n - Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.\n\n - Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.\n\n - Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.\n\n - Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist\n\n - Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.\n\n - Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.\n\n - Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.\n\n - Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.\n\n - Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.\n\n - (If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).\n\n - Perform other duties as assigned.\n\nWhat we are looking for\n\n - Active, unrestricted, and independent license to provide mental health treatment from at least one US state. Will consider pre-licensed candidates for Pacific and Mountain time zones.\n\n - Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.\n\n - Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.\n\n - Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.\n\n - Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.\n\n - Spanish speaking and able to provide care in Spanish\n\nHow we support you\n\n - Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care\n\n - We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - A 401k to save for you future\n\n - Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need\n\n - Malpractice insurance covered by us!\n\n - We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients\n\nWorking days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.\n\nThis posting is part of our evergreen talent pipeline. We welcome resumes year-round because we frequently open new positions for this role as we grow. Even if we are not hiring at this exact moment, submitting your application now allows our recruiters to review your experience, keep you top-of-mind, and reach out quickly when the next opening becomes available. If you’re a strong match, we’ll contact you to discuss timing and next steps—otherwise we’ll keep your information on file and revisit it each time a new need arises.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$55K – $75K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$55K - $75K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"30944cc4-ac30-48be-bb8d-75636347c0c6","tierSummary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"102198d9-6c8b-459e-abe1-2ea72e542b8c","summary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}},{"id":"cb8e7116-fa4b-48e6-88e1-39ba89704774","title":"Behavioral Health Care Manager","department":"Providers","team":"Providers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-29T22:03:01.674+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/cb8e7116-fa4b-48e6-88e1-39ba89704774","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/cb8e7116-fa4b-48e6-88e1-39ba89704774/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Protocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Through a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will be doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform other duties as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted license to provide mental health treatment in at least one U.S. state preferred; however, pre-licensed candidates are also accepted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plus if certified proficient for practice in Spanish or Mandarin.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A 401k to save for you future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Malpractice insurance covered by us!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Protocol Behavioral Health\n\nProtocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.\n\nAbout the role\n\nThrough a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\n - Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.\n\n - Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.\n\n - Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.\n\n - Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.\n\n - Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist\n\n - Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.\n\n - Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.\n\n - Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.\n\n - Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.\n\n - Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.\n\n - (If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).\n\n - Perform other duties as assigned.\n\nWhat we are looking for\n\n - Active, unrestricted license to provide mental health treatment in at least one U.S. state preferred; however, pre-licensed candidates are also accepted.\n\n - Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.\n\n - Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.\n\n - Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.\n\n - Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.\n\n - Plus if certified proficient for practice in Spanish or Mandarin.\n\nHow we support you\n\n - Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care\n\n - We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - A 401k to save for you future\n\n - Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need\n\n - Malpractice insurance covered by us!\n\n - We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients\n\nWorking days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.\n\n\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$55K – $75K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$55K - $75K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"24bc5f1d-5195-443e-8eab-1a18d64140c2","tierSummary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6a7ae00b-9d63-45d3-ac44-8c9a392d82f2","summary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}},{"id":"29be98e3-fc6f-4321-8780-d151160a530c","title":"Director of Partner Success","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago, IL","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-13T21:28:47.592+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"IL","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/29be98e3-fc6f-4321-8780-d151160a530c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/29be98e3-fc6f-4321-8780-d151160a530c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Protocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are: emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The team consists of experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We are a fast-growing, early-stage company focused on expanding access to care through strong partnerships with leading oncology providers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is central to how Protocol grows and sustains its impact. We partner with oncology clinics and cancer centers to deliver behavioral health care to cancer patients, and the success of that model depends on two things working well together: strong, trusted relationships with our oncology practice partners and a healthy patient referral pipeline that converts referred patients into care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to our Chief Executive Officer, this person will serve as the primary relationship owner for our oncology practice partners, partnering with our internal implementation team to ensure a clean handoff once each practice is live, then owning account management, driving performance, and ensuring partners have a high-quality experience working with Protocol. In parallel, they will work to activate referring providers within those partnerships and oversee the patient referral funnel, leading the Care Coordinator team in converting referred patients to scheduled and completed intakes with a Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is well-suited for someone who is growth-oriented and relationship-driven in equal measure, energized by moving referral numbers, building trust with clinical partners, and doing the operational work that makes both possible. Comfort with early-stage environments and a genuine connection to the mission of improving access to behavioral health care for cancer patients are a must.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>In this role you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own ongoing relationships with oncology practice partners, serving as their primary point of contact at Protocol</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and lead quarterly Joint Operating Committee (JOC) meetings with practice partners, including performance reporting and workflow optimization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor and report on partnership performance metrics, providing actionable insights to partner practices and internal leadership to drive continuous improvement across accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Activate referring providers within implemented clinic and practice partnerships, building and maintaining relationships to drive consistent inbound referral flow to Protocol</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Re-engage lapsed or low-volume referrers and address barriers preventing consistent utilization of Protocol services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and manage the Care Coordinator team, overseeing their effectiveness in converting referred patients to scheduled and completed intakes with a Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive and own referral volume and patient conversion from referral through completed intake by developing and managing patient &amp; clinician facing content and reporting that move providers to refer patients to engage, including outreach scripting, provider education and partner dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with clinical and operations teams to coordinate panel reviews between BHCMs and their most frequent clinical partners, while designing and building the systems, processes, and infrastructure that support scalable partner success and referral conversion as Protocol grows</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who are we looking for?</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7–10+ years of experience in healthcare operations, customer success, partner management, business development, or a similar growth-oriented or relationship-driven role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A growth mindset and a track record of moving numbers across referral volume, pipeline, and patient conversion, with a genuine drive to build, not just maintain</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to manage and grow complex partnerships with clinical or operational stakeholders, including at the executive level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing a team and developing frontline staff, with a track record of driving team performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with clinical, operational, and executive stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong problem-solving mindset, with sound judgment and the ability to navigate complex operational challenges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced, early-stage environment, with adaptability to ambiguity and ongoing change</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to use data to track performance, drive accountability, and inform decisions across both the partner and patient funnel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a role that required both relationship management and operational execution</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare services, oncology, or a related specialty care setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the collaborative care model or integrated behavioral health in a specialty care setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working directly with clinical staff, practice administrators, or oncology care teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in an early-stage or high-growth healthcare services company</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why work at Protocol?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working at Protocol Behavioral Health means joining a purpose-driven team at the forefront of transforming cancer care through compassionate, integrated mental health support. Every team member plays a vital role in addressing one of the most overlooked challenges in oncology: ensuring patients have timely access to high-quality behavioral health care. With a leadership team composed of seasoned experts from top healthcare and behavioral health organizations, Protocol offers a rare opportunity to learn from the best while helping build something truly meaningful from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We foster a collaborative, mission-first culture where innovation, empathy, and excellence are not just encouraged, they’re expected. Employees benefit from flexible hybrid work, competitive healthcare coverage, generous paid time off, and the fulfillment of knowing their work directly improves lives. If you’re looking to grow professionally while making a tangible difference in healthcare, Protocol could be a great fit for you.</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Protocol Behavioral Health\n\nProtocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are: emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.\n\nThe team consists of experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We are a fast-growing, early-stage company focused on expanding access to care through strong partnerships with leading oncology providers.\n\n\n\nAbout the role\n\nThis role is central to how Protocol grows and sustains its impact. We partner with oncology clinics and cancer centers to deliver behavioral health care to cancer patients, and the success of that model depends on two things working well together: strong, trusted relationships with our oncology practice partners and a healthy patient referral pipeline that converts referred patients into care.\n\nReporting to our Chief Executive Officer, this person will serve as the primary relationship owner for our oncology practice partners, partnering with our internal implementation team to ensure a clean handoff once each practice is live, then owning account management, driving performance, and ensuring partners have a high-quality experience working with Protocol. In parallel, they will work to activate referring providers within those partnerships and oversee the patient referral funnel, leading the Care Coordinator team in converting referred patients to scheduled and completed intakes with a Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM).\n\nThis role is well-suited for someone who is growth-oriented and relationship-driven in equal measure, energized by moving referral numbers, building trust with clinical partners, and doing the operational work that makes both possible. Comfort with early-stage environments and a genuine connection to the mission of improving access to behavioral health care for cancer patients are a must.\n\n\n\nIn this role you will:\n\n - Own ongoing relationships with oncology practice partners, serving as their primary point of contact at Protocol\n\n - Plan and lead quarterly Joint Operating Committee (JOC) meetings with practice partners, including performance reporting and workflow optimization\n\n - Monitor and report on partnership performance metrics, providing actionable insights to partner practices and internal leadership to drive continuous improvement across accounts\n\n - Activate referring providers within implemented clinic and practice partnerships, building and maintaining relationships to drive consistent inbound referral flow to Protocol\n\n - Re-engage lapsed or low-volume referrers and address barriers preventing consistent utilization of Protocol services\n\n - Lead and manage the Care Coordinator team, overseeing their effectiveness in converting referred patients to scheduled and completed intakes with a Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM)\n\n - Drive and own referral volume and patient conversion from referral through completed intake by developing and managing patient & clinician facing content and reporting that move providers to refer patients to engage, including outreach scripting, provider education and partner dashboards\n\n - Work cross-functionally with clinical and operations teams to coordinate panel reviews between BHCMs and their most frequent clinical partners, while designing and building the systems, processes, and infrastructure that support scalable partner success and referral conversion as Protocol grows\n   \n   \n\nWho are we looking for?\n\n - 7–10+ years of experience in healthcare operations, customer success, partner management, business development, or a similar growth-oriented or relationship-driven role\n\n - A growth mindset and a track record of moving numbers across referral volume, pipeline, and patient conversion, with a genuine drive to build, not just maintain\n\n - Proven ability to manage and grow complex partnerships with clinical or operational stakeholders, including at the executive level\n\n - Experience managing a team and developing frontline staff, with a track record of driving team performance\n\n - Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with clinical, operational, and executive stakeholders\n\n - A strong problem-solving mindset, with sound judgment and the ability to navigate complex operational challenges\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced, early-stage environment, with adaptability to ambiguity and ongoing change\n\n - Ability to use data to track performance, drive accountability, and inform decisions across both the partner and patient funnel\n\n - Experience in a role that required both relationship management and operational execution\n   \n   \n\nPreferred qualifications\n\n - Experience in healthcare services, oncology, or a related specialty care setting\n\n - Familiarity with the collaborative care model or integrated behavioral health in a specialty care setting\n\n - Experience working directly with clinical staff, practice administrators, or oncology care teams\n\n - Background in an early-stage or high-growth healthcare services company\n   \n   \n\nWhy work at Protocol?\n\nWorking at Protocol Behavioral Health means joining a purpose-driven team at the forefront of transforming cancer care through compassionate, integrated mental health support. Every team member plays a vital role in addressing one of the most overlooked challenges in oncology: ensuring patients have timely access to high-quality behavioral health care. With a leadership team composed of seasoned experts from top healthcare and behavioral health organizations, Protocol offers a rare opportunity to learn from the best while helping build something truly meaningful from the ground up.\n\nWe foster a collaborative, mission-first culture where innovation, empathy, and excellence are not just encouraged, they’re expected. Employees benefit from flexible hybrid work, competitive healthcare coverage, generous paid time off, and the fulfillment of knowing their work directly improves lives. If you’re looking to grow professionally while making a tangible difference in healthcare, Protocol could be a great fit for you.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$145K – $175K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$145K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b9dc7b79-8d55-4084-ab8f-07b556dc9894","tierSummary":"$145K – $175K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0021a76e-3ec3-411d-ba07-8851ebc7439f","summary":"$145K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":145000,"maxValue":175000}]}},{"id":"0461bcc1-26b6-4a3d-a045-8c2ac35c1acf","title":"Behavioral Health Care Manager - Pacific Time Zone","department":"Providers","team":"Providers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T21:46:02.603+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/0461bcc1-26b6-4a3d-a045-8c2ac35c1acf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/0461bcc1-26b6-4a3d-a045-8c2ac35c1acf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Protocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Through a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will be doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform other duties as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted license to provide mental health treatment in at least one U.S. state preferred; however, pre-licensed candidates are also accepted.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Available to work PST time zone between 8:30a - 5:00pm</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plus if certified proficient for practice in Spanish or Mandarin.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A 401k to save for you future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Malpractice insurance covered by us!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Protocol Behavioral Health\n\nProtocol provides cancer-specific behavioral health treatment to patients by partnering with oncology clinics and cancer centers. Oncology patients are at heightened risk of mental health disorders and suicide, and those conditions negatively impact patient outcomes, treatment adherence, and total cost of care. Our approach is designed to meet patients where they are—emotionally, logistically, and financially. We deliver high-quality mental health support for cancer patients using the collaborative care model, integrated directly into oncology treatment centers.\n\nAbout the role\n\nThrough a Collaborative Care Model partnership with oncology clinics, the Behavioral Health Care Manager (BHCM) is responsible for providing evidence-based treatment (e.g., cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy, acceptance and commitment therapy among others) to patients with cancer. The BHCM is responsible for treatment delivery via telehealth (video and phone), documentation and communication with oncology teams, consultation with the Protocol consulting psychiatrist, maintenance of the patient registry, and ongoing assessment of patient progress.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\n - Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.\n\n - Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.\n\n - Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.\n\n - Maintain a patient registry aligned with requirements of the Collaborative Care Model.\n\n - Participate in weekly consultation meetings with Protocol’s consulting psychiatrist\n\n - Communicate and collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations and attend care coordination meetings as needed.\n\n - Maintain a patient caseload targeting 65% patient-facing time.\n\n - Participate in initial and ongoing training required by Protocol.\n\n - Utilize between-session messaging as indicated to support patients.\n\n - Engage in ongoing supervision and department meetings.\n\n - (If licensed) maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).\n\n - Perform other duties as assigned.\n\nWhat we are looking for\n\n - Active, unrestricted license to provide mental health treatment in at least one U.S. state preferred; however, pre-licensed candidates are also accepted.\n\n - Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity.\n\n - Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting.\n\n - Experience with patients with oncology and/or chronic/serious medical conditions.\n\n - Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma.\n\n - Available to work PST time zone between 8:30a - 5:00pm\n\n - Plus if certified proficient for practice in Spanish or Mandarin.\n\nHow we support you\n\n - Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care\n\n - We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - A 401k to save for you future\n\n - Flexible paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need\n\n - Malpractice insurance covered by us!\n\n - We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients\n\nWorking days/hours will be discussed individually to meet patient needs for Protocol’s partnerships with cancer centers.\n\n\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$55K – $75K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$55K - $75K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4fdf95b0-db5c-421b-8c61-65e0fdcd6c68","tierSummary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a264c83b-e1a9-4124-8f6b-e0eb22105e2a","summary":"Salary within range varies based on experience and licensure $55K – $75K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":75000}]}},{"id":"27f16e2b-0522-4bba-b5c0-650daee55918","title":"Lead Behavioral Health Care Manager","department":"Clinical","team":"Clinical","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T21:47:20.180+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/27f16e2b-0522-4bba-b5c0-650daee55918","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/27f16e2b-0522-4bba-b5c0-650daee55918/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Lead Behavioral Health Care Manager is an experienced, licensed Behavioral Healthcare Manager (BHCM) responsible for clinical supervision and management of a team of BHCMs, as well as delivering some direct patient care. You will collaborate with clinical leadership to support clinical supervision for evidence-based treatments delivered via the Collaborative Care Model (CoCM) to cancer patients. The best candidate for this role is data-driven and outcomes-focused who understands how to bring out the highest quality work in their team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will be doing</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a team of BHCMs with the following responsibilities (70% of your time):</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training as needed to BHCMs to deliver evidence-based treatments to cancer patients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review BHCM sessions for quality assessments and provide feedback to BHCMs for improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track KPIs of BHCMs and support them in achieving targets, such as timely completion of documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct audits of session notes to ensure compliant documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively identify challenges for BHCMs and identify solutions in collaboration with clinical leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in rotating business hours on-call for patient safety concerns and risk-assessments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate BHCMs job performance and develop improvement plans as needed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct direct patient care via Collaborative Care Model (40% of your time), which includes:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In accordance CoCM, maintain a patient registry, participate in weekly consultations with psychiatrist, and communicate &amp; collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform other duties as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Licensed mental health providers with 2+ years experience treating patients with chronic/serious medical illness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years of experience leading a team. A plus if experience managing a remote team across multiple states</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent use of data to support decision-making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong skills in communication and working on diverse teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to balance business needs with clinical priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort in a fast-paced environment with frequent change</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ability to work virtual clinic hours in the Pacific Timezone</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A 401k to save for you future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Malpractice insurance covered by us!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why work at Protocol?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working at Protocol Behavioral Health means joining a purpose-driven team at the forefront of transforming cancer care through compassionate, integrated mental health support. Every team member plays a vital role in addressing one of the most overlooked challenges in oncology: ensuring patients have timely access to high-quality behavioral health care. With a leadership team composed of seasoned experts from top healthcare and behavioral health organizations, Protocol offers a rare opportunity to learn from the best while helping build something truly meaningful from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We foster a collaborative, mission-first culture where innovation, empathy, and excellence are not just encouraged, they’re expected. Employees benefit from flexible hybrid work, competitive healthcare coverage, generous paid time off, and the fulfillment of knowing their work directly improves lives. If you’re looking to grow professionally while making a tangible difference in healthcare, Protocol could be a great fit for you.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT PROTOCOL BEHAVIORAL HEALTH\n\nOur mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.\n\nA cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.\n\nOur team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.\n\nAbout the role\n\nThe Lead Behavioral Health Care Manager is an experienced, licensed Behavioral Healthcare Manager (BHCM) responsible for clinical supervision and management of a team of BHCMs, as well as delivering some direct patient care. You will collaborate with clinical leadership to support clinical supervision for evidence-based treatments delivered via the Collaborative Care Model (CoCM) to cancer patients. The best candidate for this role is data-driven and outcomes-focused who understands how to bring out the highest quality work in their team.\n\nWhat you will be doing\n\nLead a team of BHCMs with the following responsibilities (70% of your time):\n\n - Provide training as needed to BHCMs to deliver evidence-based treatments to cancer patients\n\n - Review BHCM sessions for quality assessments and provide feedback to BHCMs for improvement\n\n - Track KPIs of BHCMs and support them in achieving targets, such as timely completion of documentation\n\n - Conduct audits of session notes to ensure compliant documentation\n\n - Proactively identify challenges for BHCMs and identify solutions in collaboration with clinical leadership\n\n - Participate in rotating business hours on-call for patient safety concerns and risk-assessments\n\n - Evaluate BHCMs job performance and develop improvement plans as needed\n\nConduct direct patient care via Collaborative Care Model (40% of your time), which includes:\n\n - Conduct structured assessments of mental and behavioral health and functioning of oncology patients referred by partner cancer centers and clinics.\n\n - Develop treatment plans based on assessment results using Protocol’s evidence-based modular treatment approach.\n\n - Implement treatment modules and conduct ongoing progress assessment to guide next steps in care and make changes as indicated by patient progress.\n\n - In accordance CoCM, maintain a patient registry, participate in weekly consultations with psychiatrist, and communicate & collaborate with oncology teams about patient progress and recommendations\n\n - Maintain licensure in home state and obtain licensure in other states as requested by Protocol (licensure costs will be covered by Protocol).\n\n - Perform other duties as assigned.\n\nWhat we are looking for\n\n - Licensed mental health providers with 2+ years experience treating patients with chronic/serious medical illness\n\n - 1+ years of experience leading a team. A plus if experience managing a remote team across multiple states\n\n - Consistent use of data to support decision-making\n\n - Strong skills in communication and working on diverse teams\n\n - Ability to balance business needs with clinical priorities\n\n - Comfort in a fast-paced environment with frequent change\n\n - Ability to support a caseload of patients of different diagnoses, backgrounds and cultures, and with varying degrees of acuity\n\n - Ability to deliver care in a virtual setting\n\n - Experience supporting patients with suicidal ideation and/or trauma\n\n - Ability to work virtual clinic hours in the Pacific Timezone\n\nHow we support you\n\n - Extensive training in evidence-based treatment modules for cancer patients and ongoing consultation and professional development opportunities aligned with psycho-oncology care\n\n - We make sure you get the care you need by providing medical, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - A 401k to save for you future\n\n - Generous paid time off so that you have the time away from work to decompress and take care of what you need\n\n - Malpractice insurance covered by us!\n\n - We cover the cost for any continued education and license renewals that are required for you to take care of our patients\n\nWhy work at Protocol?\n\nWorking at Protocol Behavioral Health means joining a purpose-driven team at the forefront of transforming cancer care through compassionate, integrated mental health support. Every team member plays a vital role in addressing one of the most overlooked challenges in oncology: ensuring patients have timely access to high-quality behavioral health care. With a leadership team composed of seasoned experts from top healthcare and behavioral health organizations, Protocol offers a rare opportunity to learn from the best while helping build something truly meaningful from the ground up.\n\nWe foster a collaborative, mission-first culture where innovation, empathy, and excellence are not just encouraged, they’re expected. Employees benefit from flexible hybrid work, competitive healthcare coverage, generous paid time off, and the fulfillment of knowing their work directly improves lives. If you’re looking to grow professionally while making a tangible difference in healthcare, Protocol could be a great fit for you.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$85K – $95K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$85K - $95K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c7377ea0-9626-4d9f-869e-b758914b8164","tierSummary":"$85K – $95K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"755d9f6e-ccd3-4a4c-9591-578f04a3cb8d","summary":"$85K – $95K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":85000,"maxValue":95000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":85000,"maxValue":95000}]}},{"id":"98bc61a5-8927-47da-8df3-9495961d7045","title":"Manager, Implementation & Operations","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T22:09:56.433+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/98bc61a5-8927-47da-8df3-9495961d7045","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/98bc61a5-8927-47da-8df3-9495961d7045/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>About the Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Manager, Implementation &amp; Operations will serve as the primary point person for new partner implementations, translating partnership structure and market-specific nuances into a clear, executable plan and driving it from kickoff through go-live and into steady-state operations. This role sits at the intersection of external partner management and internal cross-functional execution, working closely with clinical, operations, and technology teams to keep workstreams aligned and launches on track.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the Senior Director, Business Operations, this role begins with project management support while learning Protocol's model directly, then transitions to independently owning implementations. The ideal candidate is a structured, proactive executor who thrives in ambiguity and owns outcomes rather than just tasks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, this role will be responsible for broader business operations initiatives outside of implementation work. Time and focus will flex between active implementations and operations projects as volume rises and falls, with room to take on higher-level ownership of select work across toolkits, playbooks, and cross-team processes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point person for new partner implementations — leading partner meetings, building and maintaining project plans, and coordinating technology setup end to end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own up to two concurrent client implementations once fully ramped, including onsite support during launch and oversight of education and marketing material delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate partnership structure and market- or partner-specific nuances into a clear, executable plan, anticipating risks early and driving mitigation plans without waiting to be asked</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex partner implementation conversations as a proactive problem solver — someone who surfaces issues and drives them to resolution, not just a project manager keeping things on track</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own implementation outcomes, not just task completion — finding the problems and having the hard conversations, not simply keeping things on track</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Refine/Iterate on current implementation project management templates and the existing implementation playbook</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flex time and focus between implementation work and business operations projects as implementation volume speeds up and slows down</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take higher-level ownership of select work currently managed by the broader operations team — including optimizing toolkits and playbooks and improving manual processes — partnering cross-functionally to increase efficiency across operations and the clinical team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Who we're looking for:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4-6 years of experience with a track record of owning implementations end to end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare implementation experience, ideally within a managed-services model; SaaS implementation experience also considered, provided there is strong operational (not just project management) ownership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of how a clinic functions, including revenue cycle fundamentals, and experience or aptitude for driving provider behavior change</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Electronic Medical Record (EMR) or Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems and the technical aspects of implementation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive problem solver who identifies issues and leads the conversations to resolve them, rather than operating solely as a project manager</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to independently drive work forward, solve problems, and manage ambiguity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable holding multiple concurrent workstreams and flexing between client-facing implementation work and internal business operations projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong project management fundamentals — building and iterating on project plans, templates, and playbooks — paired with excellent relationship-management and communication skills to lead partner-facing meetings independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to travel 20%-30% as needed to support onsite launches and partner meetings</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Preferred qualifications:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in oncology, behavioral health, or value-based care settings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a high-growth, early-stage healthcare services startup environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in management consulting within healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience performance analyses and translating data/findings into operational workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entrepreneurial spirit</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Why work at Protocol?</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working at Protocol Behavioral Health means joining a purpose-driven team at the forefront of transforming cancer care through compassionate, integrated mental health support. Every team member plays a vital role in addressing one of the most overlooked challenges in oncology: ensuring patients have timely access to high-quality behavioral health care. With a leadership team composed of seasoned experts from top healthcare and behavioral health organizations, Protocol offers a rare opportunity to learn from the best while helping build something truly meaningful from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We foster a collaborative, mission-first culture where innovation, empathy, and excellence are not just encouraged, they’re expected. Employees benefit from flexible hybrid work, competitive healthcare coverage, generous paid time off, and the fulfillment of knowing their work directly improves lives. If you’re looking to grow professionally while making a tangible difference in healthcare, Protocol could be a great fit for you.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT PROTOCOL BEHAVIORAL HEALTH\n\nOur mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.\n\nA cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.\n\nOur team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThe Manager, Implementation & Operations will serve as the primary point person for new partner implementations, translating partnership structure and market-specific nuances into a clear, executable plan and driving it from kickoff through go-live and into steady-state operations. This role sits at the intersection of external partner management and internal cross-functional execution, working closely with clinical, operations, and technology teams to keep workstreams aligned and launches on track.\n\nReporting to the Senior Director, Business Operations, this role begins with project management support while learning Protocol's model directly, then transitions to independently owning implementations. The ideal candidate is a structured, proactive executor who thrives in ambiguity and owns outcomes rather than just tasks.\n\nAdditionally, this role will be responsible for broader business operations initiatives outside of implementation work. Time and focus will flex between active implementations and operations projects as volume rises and falls, with room to take on higher-level ownership of select work across toolkits, playbooks, and cross-team processes.\n\n\n\n\nIN THIS ROLE, YOU WILL:\n\n - Serve as the primary point person for new partner implementations — leading partner meetings, building and maintaining project plans, and coordinating technology setup end to end\n\n - Own up to two concurrent client implementations once fully ramped, including onsite support during launch and oversight of education and marketing material delivery\n\n - Translate partnership structure and market- or partner-specific nuances into a clear, executable plan, anticipating risks early and driving mitigation plans without waiting to be asked\n\n - Lead complex partner implementation conversations as a proactive problem solver — someone who surfaces issues and drives them to resolution, not just a project manager keeping things on track\n\n - Own implementation outcomes, not just task completion — finding the problems and having the hard conversations, not simply keeping things on track\n\n - Refine/Iterate on current implementation project management templates and the existing implementation playbook\n\n - Flex time and focus between implementation work and business operations projects as implementation volume speeds up and slows down\n\n - Take higher-level ownership of select work currently managed by the broader operations team — including optimizing toolkits and playbooks and improving manual processes — partnering cross-functionally to increase efficiency across operations and the clinical team\n\n\n\n\nWHO WE'RE LOOKING FOR:\n\n - 4-6 years of experience with a track record of owning implementations end to end\n\n - Healthcare implementation experience, ideally within a managed-services model; SaaS implementation experience also considered, provided there is strong operational (not just project management) ownership\n\n - Working knowledge of how a clinic functions, including revenue cycle fundamentals, and experience or aptitude for driving provider behavior change\n\n - Familiarity with Electronic Medical Record (EMR) or Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems and the technical aspects of implementation\n\n - A proactive problem solver who identifies issues and leads the conversations to resolve them, rather than operating solely as a project manager\n\n - Demonstrated ability to independently drive work forward, solve problems, and manage ambiguity\n\n - Comfortable holding multiple concurrent workstreams and flexing between client-facing implementation work and internal business operations projects\n\n - Strong project management fundamentals — building and iterating on project plans, templates, and playbooks — paired with excellent relationship-management and communication skills to lead partner-facing meetings independently\n\n - Ability to travel 20%-30% as needed to support onsite launches and partner meetings\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:\n\n - Prior experience in oncology, behavioral health, or value-based care settings\n\n - Experience in a high-growth, early-stage healthcare services startup environment\n\n - Background in management consulting within healthcare\n\n - Experience performance analyses and translating data/findings into operational workflows\n\n - Entrepreneurial spirit\n\n\n\n\nWHY WORK AT PROTOCOL?\n\nWorking at Protocol Behavioral Health means joining a purpose-driven team at the forefront of transforming cancer care through compassionate, integrated mental health support. Every team member plays a vital role in addressing one of the most overlooked challenges in oncology: ensuring patients have timely access to high-quality behavioral health care. With a leadership team composed of seasoned experts from top healthcare and behavioral health organizations, Protocol offers a rare opportunity to learn from the best while helping build something truly meaningful from the ground up.\n\nWe foster a collaborative, mission-first culture where innovation, empathy, and excellence are not just encouraged, they’re expected. Employees benefit from flexible hybrid work, competitive healthcare coverage, generous paid time off, and the fulfillment of knowing their work directly improves lives. If you’re looking to grow professionally while making a tangible difference in healthcare, Protocol could be a great fit for you.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$95K – $115K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$95K - $115K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9dac614e-8a55-4844-a3e1-2b0bd273b590","tierSummary":"$95K – $115K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"eb637d31-0812-4633-a8f8-bd9c91c1f128","summary":"$95K – $115K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":95000,"maxValue":115000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":95000,"maxValue":115000}]}},{"id":"d7516e25-ef53-4afa-906e-f1c1f575cfca","title":"Patient Engagement Coordinator - Contractor","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T21:56:11.705+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/d7516e25-ef53-4afa-906e-f1c1f575cfca","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/d7516e25-ef53-4afa-906e-f1c1f575cfca/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Patient Engagement Coordinator is the first voice a patient hears when they're referred into our program, and the person responsible for making sure that referral actually turns into care. You'll guide patients from the moment they're referred all the way through to their first intake — answering questions, building trust, walking them through consent, and getting them scheduled with a Behavioral Health Care Manager.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">But getting someone to care once isn't the finish line. Patients cancel, miss appointments, or drift away for all kinds of reasons and when they do, they don't just fall off a list. They become your responsibility. You'll reach back out, understand what got in the way, and help them find their way back into the care they need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is about ownership of outcomes, not just activity: every referral that becomes a completed intake, and every patient who re-engages instead of falling through the cracks, is a patient who got the care they need because of you - a win you're accountable for.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the patient conversion funnel, ensuring referrals are contacted within our SLAs to ensure timely access to care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead omnichannel outreach to new patient referrals, initiating contact across phone and text to introduce Protocol’s program, explain how it works, and answer patient questions to ensure patients feel supported and informed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle common objections and hesitations with empathy and confidence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk patients through informed consent and ensure documentation is completed accurately</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule patients for their intake session and confirm attendance, handling reminders and reschedules as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work a recurring list of unengaged patients — cancellations, no-shows, and program drop-offs — to understand what got in the way and bring them back into care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Re-educate and re-motivate disengaged patients on the value of the program, re-scheduling and re-consenting as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track outreach activity and outcomes in the CRM/EHR, and report on key metrics:  referral-to-outreach time, outreach-to-scheduled-intake time, referral-to-scheduled-intake conversion rate, and completed intakes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Clinical &amp; Operations teams to hand off scheduled patients cleanly and surface recurring friction points that could improve messaging or process</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a phone-based customer service, call center, sales development, or patient-facing healthcare coordination role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable being held to conversion and pipeline targets, not just call counts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator who can educate, build trust, and overcome objections without being pushy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and detail-oriented — able to manage a live pipeline of referrals and a separate re-engagement queue simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empathetic and patient, especially with patients who are confused, frustrated, or hesitant</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with CRM/EHR systems and documenting consent accurately</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare, medical sales, or patient enrollment experience a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual (Spanish) a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Compensation</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a 1099 contracted role</strong> at a rate between $20-$24 an hour with potential to a full-time opportunity</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT PROTOCOL BEHAVIORAL HEALTH\n\nOur mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.\n\nA cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.\n\nOur team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThe Patient Engagement Coordinator is the first voice a patient hears when they're referred into our program, and the person responsible for making sure that referral actually turns into care. You'll guide patients from the moment they're referred all the way through to their first intake — answering questions, building trust, walking them through consent, and getting them scheduled with a Behavioral Health Care Manager.\n\nBut getting someone to care once isn't the finish line. Patients cancel, miss appointments, or drift away for all kinds of reasons and when they do, they don't just fall off a list. They become your responsibility. You'll reach back out, understand what got in the way, and help them find their way back into the care they need.\n\nThis role is about ownership of outcomes, not just activity: every referral that becomes a completed intake, and every patient who re-engages instead of falling through the cracks, is a patient who got the care they need because of you - a win you're accountable for.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Own the patient conversion funnel, ensuring referrals are contacted within our SLAs to ensure timely access to care\n\n - Lead omnichannel outreach to new patient referrals, initiating contact across phone and text to introduce Protocol’s program, explain how it works, and answer patient questions to ensure patients feel supported and informed\n\n - Handle common objections and hesitations with empathy and confidence\n\n - Walk patients through informed consent and ensure documentation is completed accurately\n\n - Schedule patients for their intake session and confirm attendance, handling reminders and reschedules as needed\n\n - Work a recurring list of unengaged patients — cancellations, no-shows, and program drop-offs — to understand what got in the way and bring them back into care\n\n - Re-educate and re-motivate disengaged patients on the value of the program, re-scheduling and re-consenting as needed\n\n - Track outreach activity and outcomes in the CRM/EHR, and report on key metrics:  referral-to-outreach time, outreach-to-scheduled-intake time, referral-to-scheduled-intake conversion rate, and completed intakes\n\n - Partner with the Clinical & Operations teams to hand off scheduled patients cleanly and surface recurring friction points that could improve messaging or process\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Experience in a phone-based customer service, call center, sales development, or patient-facing healthcare coordination role\n\n - Comfortable being held to conversion and pipeline targets, not just call counts\n\n - Strong communicator who can educate, build trust, and overcome objections without being pushy\n\n - Organized and detail-oriented — able to manage a live pipeline of referrals and a separate re-engagement queue simultaneously\n\n - Empathetic and patient, especially with patients who are confused, frustrated, or hesitant\n\n - Comfortable with CRM/EHR systems and documenting consent accurately\n\n - Healthcare, medical sales, or patient enrollment experience a plus\n\n - Bilingual (Spanish) a plus\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nThis is a 1099 contracted role at a rate between $20-$24 an hour with potential to a full-time opportunity","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$20 – $24 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"4318b1f7-3562-4e1c-86c2-1d88e6fa340c","tierSummary":"$20 – $24 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4cb52dba-b598-4411-9cd1-15de3cacf5eb","summary":"$20 – $24 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20,"maxValue":24}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20,"maxValue":24}]}},{"id":"eed48b3e-3205-4447-b749-6695087bcb1c","title":"Director, Sales & Marketing","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chicago, IL","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T22:32:01.823+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"IL","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Chicago"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/eed48b3e-3205-4447-b749-6695087bcb1c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/protocol-cares/eed48b3e-3205-4447-b749-6695087bcb1c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Protocol Behavioral Health</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>About the Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Director, Sales &amp; Marketing plays a critical role in supporting Protocol's growth by driving the execution, infrastructure, and marketing behind our go-to-market efforts. This role operates at the center of Protocol's commercial function, working closely with leadership to manage pipeline activity, take the lead on marketing, and advance high-priority company objectives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to our Chief Commercial Officer, this is a hands-on, individual-contributor role for someone who can move fluidly between shaping priorities with leadership and executing the work directly, using technology and AI tools to extend their own reach and get more done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is well suited for a highly analytical, organized operator who thrives in ambiguity and wants to help shape what this function becomes</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In this role you will:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and build Protocol's growth infrastructure, including CRM, pipeline management, forecasting, and reporting, ensuring clear visibility into pipeline performance, conversion, and deal velocity, and manage the full sales cycle from lead through signed contract</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take the lead on marketing for Protocol, building out top-of-funnel activity, a reusable content library, and the outbound/inbound engine (HubSpot automation, content distribution, conference strategy) needed to keep the funnel full and drive continued engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build financial and operational models and develop business cases to evaluate new partnerships, expansion opportunities, and growth initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the Chief Commercial Officer &amp; senior leadership team to translate growth priorities into structured execution plans, driving progress across key initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the exec team in owning cross-functional initiatives, preparing board and leadership materials, and helping run operating cadences, planning processes, and offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve Protocol's external narrative, including decks, one-pagers, case studies, and partner-facing materials, ensuring consistency, quality, and a compelling value proposition</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead branding and marketing initiatives, including a messaging guide, campaign execution, and potential rebrand efforts to strengthen go-to-market effectiveness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify bottlenecks across growth, marketing, and operations, and implement process improvements and scalable systems that increase efficiency, consistency, and speed</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who we're looking for:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4 to 8+ years of experience in business operations, growth marketing, sales operations, business development, consulting, or healthcare services operations, with direct, hands-on experience owning marketing execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> Equally comfortable in a strategy conversation with executives and doing the hands-on work of building a campaign or writing outbound copy; strong analytical and financial modeling skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with CRM and marketing automation systems such as HubSpot or Salesforce, with a strong understanding of pipeline management, segmentation, and data integrity; CRM implementation experience a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using technology and AI tools to extend their own reach and get more done</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and drive complex processes forward</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, including experience preparing presentations, business cases, or executive-facing materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High level of ownership, operational rigor, and comfort working in ambiguity while building scalable processes and infrastructure from scratch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal skills and comfort moving between executive-level conversations and hands-on engagement with external partners</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred qualifications:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare services, specialty physician services, oncology, urology, radiation, or practice operations, or a high-growth healthcare services startup environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working cross-functionally with leadership teams on strategic initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HubSpot implementation or administration experience specifically</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT PROTOCOL BEHAVIORAL HEALTH\n\nOur mission is to make cancer care better for patients, providers, and payers — improving outcomes through specialized behavioral health and supportive care, embedded within oncology care teams.\n\nA cancer diagnosis changes everything, not just a patient's physical health, and we exist to make sure their emotional needs are met alongside their treatment, not as an afterthought. We do this by partnering directly with oncology clinics and cancer centers and using the collaborative care model to bring mental health support into the room where cancer care already happens. That means patients get support earlier and more consistently and providers get a partner equipped to handle the mental health care their patients need.\n\nOur team is built by experienced healthcare operators and executives who have built and scaled partnerships across behavioral health, oncology, and value-based care. We're a fast-growing, early-stage company, and every new partnership moves us closer to making specialized behavioral health a standard part of cancer care.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThe Director, Sales & Marketing plays a critical role in supporting Protocol's growth by driving the execution, infrastructure, and marketing behind our go-to-market efforts. This role operates at the center of Protocol's commercial function, working closely with leadership to manage pipeline activity, take the lead on marketing, and advance high-priority company objectives.\n\nReporting to our Chief Commercial Officer, this is a hands-on, individual-contributor role for someone who can move fluidly between shaping priorities with leadership and executing the work directly, using technology and AI tools to extend their own reach and get more done.\n\nThis role is well suited for a highly analytical, organized operator who thrives in ambiguity and wants to help shape what this function becomes\n\n\n\n\nIN THIS ROLE YOU WILL:\n\n - Own and build Protocol's growth infrastructure, including CRM, pipeline management, forecasting, and reporting, ensuring clear visibility into pipeline performance, conversion, and deal velocity, and manage the full sales cycle from lead through signed contract\n\n - Take the lead on marketing for Protocol, building out top-of-funnel activity, a reusable content library, and the outbound/inbound engine (HubSpot automation, content distribution, conference strategy) needed to keep the funnel full and drive continued engagement\n\n - Build financial and operational models and develop business cases to evaluate new partnerships, expansion opportunities, and growth initiatives\n\n - Partner closely with the Chief Commercial Officer & senior leadership team to translate growth priorities into structured execution plans, driving progress across key initiatives\n\n - Support the exec team in owning cross-functional initiatives, preparing board and leadership materials, and helping run operating cadences, planning processes, and offsites\n\n - Own and evolve Protocol's external narrative, including decks, one-pagers, case studies, and partner-facing materials, ensuring consistency, quality, and a compelling value proposition\n\n - Lead branding and marketing initiatives, including a messaging guide, campaign execution, and potential rebrand efforts to strengthen go-to-market effectiveness\n\n - Identify bottlenecks across growth, marketing, and operations, and implement process improvements and scalable systems that increase efficiency, consistency, and speed\n\n\nWHO WE'RE LOOKING FOR:\n\n - 4 to 8+ years of experience in business operations, growth marketing, sales operations, business development, consulting, or healthcare services operations, with direct, hands-on experience owning marketing execution\n\n -  Equally comfortable in a strategy conversation with executives and doing the hands-on work of building a campaign or writing outbound copy; strong analytical and financial modeling skills\n\n - Experience working with CRM and marketing automation systems such as HubSpot or Salesforce, with a strong understanding of pipeline management, segmentation, and data integrity; CRM implementation experience a plus\n\n - Comfortable using technology and AI tools to extend their own reach and get more done\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and drive complex processes forward\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, including experience preparing presentations, business cases, or executive-facing materials\n\n - High level of ownership, operational rigor, and comfort working in ambiguity while building scalable processes and infrastructure from scratch\n\n - Strong interpersonal skills and comfort moving between executive-level conversations and hands-on engagement with external partners\n\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:\n\n - Experience in healthcare services, specialty physician services, oncology, urology, radiation, or practice operations, or a high-growth healthcare services startup environment\n\n - Experience working cross-functionally with leadership teams on strategic initiatives\n\n - HubSpot implementation or administration experience specifically","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}